<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aitakkama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aitakkama was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Kadesh</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhetaten">Amarna</a> period in the 14th century BCE. Letters from Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-archive">Amarna archive</a> accuse him of going over to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and raiding neighbours loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Under Hittite protection Kadesh remained a vassal kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hatti">Hatti</a>, and Aitakkama is one of the best-documented Syrian princes of the age.</p></div>
